{"units": [{"id": "epistamai-quote14", "translation": "I know how to speak many purifications and where it is right to be silent likewise."}, {"id": "epistamai-quote15", "translation": "But you bring him in as you know how."}, {"id": "epistamai-quote16", "translation": "As I know."}, {"id": "epistamai-quote17", "translation": "First, you do not know how to be a stranger."}, {"id": "epistamai-quote18", "translation": "I know how to praise a race, having learned it."}, {"id": "epistamai-quote19", "translation": "strength (of Aeschylus) – a Mede knowing."}, {"id": "epistamai-word1", "translation": "you know"}, {"id": "epistamai-word2", "translation": "you know"}, {"id": "epistamai-word3", "translation": "I knew"}, {"id": "epistateo-orth1", "translation": "to preside over"}, {"id": "epistateo-def1", "translation": "I preside over"}, {"id": "epistateo-quote1", "translation": "But no healer presides over this speech."}, {"id": "epistatis-orth1", "translation": "commander"}, {"id": "epistatis-def1", "translation": "commander"}, {"id": "epistatis-quote1", "translation": "And the commanders, two generals."}, {"id": "epistatis-quote2", "translation": "Every man, lord of the oar, went to the ship, and every commander of arms."}, {"id": "episteicho-orth1", "translation": "to approach"}, {"id": "episteicho-def1", "translation": "I approach"}, {"id": "episteicho-quote1", "translation": "And the blasts of winds blowing sunnily approach the land."}, {"id": "epistello-orth1", "translation": "to command"}, {"id": "epistello-def1", "translation": "I command"}, {"id": "epistello-quote1", "translation": "And I commanded them to approach these houses as suppliants."}, {"id": "epistello-quote2", "translation": "Thus it has been commanded to speak about this."}, {"id": "epistello-quote3", "translation": "To whom the task has been assigned."}, {"id": "epistello-quote4", "translation": "Do what has been commanded."}, {"id": "epistello-quote5", "translation": "Whoever of the judges has been assigned this task."}, {"id": "epistenazo-orth1", "translation": "to groan over"}, {"id": "epistenazo-def1", "translation": "I groan over"}, {"id": "epistenazo-quote1", "translation": "And why do you groan over them for what they have done?"}, {"id": "epistenacho-orth1", "translation": "to groan over"}, {"id": "epistenacho-def1", "translation": "I groan over"}, {"id": "epistenacho-quote1", "translation": "Everyone is ready to groan over the unfortunate."}, {"id": "epistoli-orth1", "translation": "command"}, {"id": "epistoli-def1", "translation": "command"}, {"id": "epistoli-note1", "translation": "where in most copies ἐπιτολάς [commands] is written: about which and about the comment of Eustathius and Thomas Magister that ἐπιστολάς [commands] is said instead of ἐπιτολάς [commands] solely for metrical necessity, see what I said in the Preface to the London edition of Prometheus, 1866, p. IX and X."}, {"id": "epistoli-quote1", "translation": "But you must heed the commands which your father gave you."}, {"id": "epistoli-quote2", "translation": "And he does not remember my commands."}, {"id": "epistoli-quote3", "translation": "Only guard these commands of your father."}, {"id": "epistoli-quote4", "translation": "Hear my commands."}, {"id": "epistoli-word1", "translation": "commands"}, {"id": "epistoli-word2", "translation": "commands"}, {"id": "epistoli-word3", "translation": "commands"}, {"id": "epistrateuo-orth1", "translation": "to march against"}, {"id": "epistrateuo-def1", "translation": "I undertake an expedition against someone"}, {"id": "epistrateuo-quote1", "translation": "And I marched against many with a great army."}, {"id": "epistreptos-orth1", "translation": "turning towards"}, {"id": "epistreptos-def1", "translation": "towards whom the eyes or minds of men are turned"}, {"id": "epistreptos-quote1", "translation": "And having founded a life turning towards the paths of children."}, {"id": "epistreptos-quote2", "translation": "Having this season turning towards mortals."}, {"id": "epistrephomai-orth1", "translation": "to turn oneself"}, {"id": "epistrephomai-def1", "translation": "I turn myself"}, {"id": "epistrephomai-quote1", "translation": "Now turn yourself along this smooth grove."}, {"id": "epistrophi-orth1", "translation": "turning, resort"}, {"id": "epistrophi-def1", "translation": "a staying, a place to which one can turn"}, {"id": "epistrophi-quote1", "translation": "He will have the city and the resorts of his ancestral homes."}, {"id": "epistrophi-quote2", "translation": "The hospitable resorts of the house."}, {"id": "epistrophi-quote3", "translation": "Spercheus river and the pastoral resorts."}, {"id": "epistrophi-quote4", "translation": "The Cilician land and the resorts of the Syrians."}, {"id": "epistrophos-orth1", "translation": "turning upon"}, {"id": "epistrophos-def1", "translation": "turning upon something"}, {"id": "epistrophos-quote1", "translation": "And he destroys the unjust man who turns upon these things."}, {"id": "epistrophoamai-orth1", "translation": "to frequent"}, {"id": "epistrophoamai-def1", "translation": "I frequent a place"}, {"id": "epistrophoamai-quote1", "translation": "The house of a perfect man frequenting it."}, {"id": "epischethein-orth1", "translation": "to hold back"}, {"id": "epischethein-def1", "translation": "See ἐπέχω."}, {"id": "epischethein-word1", "translation": "I hold back"}, {"id": "epitello-orth1", "translation": "to rise"}, {"id": "epitello-def1", "translation": "I rise, I appear"}, {"id": "epitello-quote1", "translation": "When must the ends of these toils arise?"}, {"id": "epitithemai-orth1", "translation": "to set upon oneself"}, {"id": "epitithemai-def1", "translation": "I set before myself"}, {"id": "epitithemai-quote1", "translation": "You set upon yourself this sacrifice and the curses of the people."}, {"id": "epitimitris-orth1", "translation": "punisher"}, {"id": "epitimitris-def1", "translation": "punisher, chastiser"}, {"id": "epitimitris-quote1", "translation": "For the punisher of these deeds is heavy."}, {"id": "epitimion-orth1", "translation": "penalty"}, {"id": "epitimion-def1", "translation": "penalty"}, {"id": "epitimion-quote1", "translation": "To take the penalty."}, {"id": "epitimion-quote2", "translation": "Seeing such penalties for these things."}, {"id": "epitonos-orth1", "translation": "intensely"}, {"id": "epitonos-def1", "translation": "intensely"}, {"id": "epitonos-quote1", "translation": "intensely (thus Turnebus for ἐπὶ τὸν ὦ) pursuing."}, {"id": "epitymbidios-orth1", "translation": "funereal"}, {"id": "epitymbidios-def1", "translation": "funereal"}, {"id": "epitymbidios-quote1", "translation": "Instead of funereal laments."}, {"id": "epitymbios-orth1", "translation": "funereal"}, {"id": "epitymbios-def1", "translation": "funereal"}, {"id": "epitymbios-quote1", "translation": "funereal praise"}, {"id": "epitymbios-quote2", "translation": "funereal lament"}, {"id": "epituchis-orth1", "translation": "successful"}, {"id": "epituchis-def1", "translation": "enjoying favorable success"}, {"id": "epituchis-quote1", "translation": "They sailed with favorable wrath."}, {"id": "epiphero-orth1", "translation": "to bring upon"}, {"id": "epiphero-def1", "translation": "I bring upon"}, {"id": "epiphero-quote1", "translation": "Lest any man coming here should bring a well-wrought spear."}, {"id": "epiphtheggomai-orth1", "translation": "to utter in response"}, {"id": "epiphtheggomai-def1", "translation": "I sound in accompaniment, I acclaim, I answer"}]}